.TH MYGREP 3 "2024-01-01" "libmyutils" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search for a pattern in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int mygrep(FILE* fp, const char* search_str, char*** matches);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mygrep
searches for lines containing
.I search_str
in the file pointed to by
.IR fp .
.PP
Matching lines are stored in the array pointed to by
.IR matches .
The caller is responsible for freeing the allocated memory.
.PP
Returns the number of matches found, or -1 on failure.
